WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.852
The Trust Services Criteria are the foundation of SOC 2.

2
00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:12.582
They provide the categories auditors use to evaluate whether controls support the commitments and system requirements included in the audit scope.

3
00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:20.275
The five criteria are Security, Availability, Processing Integrity, Confidentiality, and Privacy.

4
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:31.809
Security is included in every SOC 2 engagement, while the other criteria are selected based on the organization's services, commitments, customer needs, and audit scope.

5
00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:43.193
Security focuses on protecting systems and information from unauthorized access, unauthorized disclosure, and damage that could affect the organization's ability to meet its objectives.

6
00:00:43.193 --> 00:00:49.250
Availability relates to whether systems are available for operation and use as committed or agreed.

7
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:57.581
It often connects to uptime, resilience, capacity management, incident response, backup, and recovery practices.

8
00:00:57.581 --> 00:01:05.324
Processing Integrity concerns whether system processing is complete, valid, accurate, timely, and authorized.

9
00:01:05.324 --> 00:01:14.643
It is most relevant when customers rely on the organization to process transactions, calculations, workflows, or data transformations correctly.

10
00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:19.642
Confidentiality focuses on protecting information designated as confidential.

11
00:01:19.642 --> 00:01:28.412
Privacy focuses on personal information and the organization's commitments around collection, use, retention, disclosure, and disposal.

12
00:01:28.412 --> 00:01:31.635
Controls connect these criteria to real activity.

13
00:01:31.635 --> 00:01:39.438
A criterion describes what needs to be supported, while controls describe how the organization manages that objective in practice.

14
00:01:39.438 --> 00:01:42.521
Choosing criteria is therefore a scoping decision.

15
00:01:42.521 --> 00:01:51.561
Organizations should understand which commitments they make to customers, what systems are included, and which criteria best reflect the service being evaluated.
